{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-009", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Flooded solar plant in Japan catches fire after typhoon", "content": "<p>A solar plant east of Tokyo caught fire in late September after typhoon floodwater submerged its electrical equipment – a post-flood risk the Japanese government has warned about since 2018.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/flooded-solar-plant-in-japan-catches-fire-after-typhoon/\">Flooded solar plant in Japan catches fire after typhoon</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/flooded-solar-plant-in-japan-catches-fire-after-typhoon/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "first_solar-2026-10-05-010", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["first_solar", "ja_solar"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.7, "reasons": ["多公司提及"]}, "title": "First Solar sues JA Solar and American Panel Solutions over TOPCon patents", "content": "<p>The largest U.S. solar manufacturer has escalated its legal push against imported TOPCon cell technology, filing a patent infringement suit in federal court against China’s JA Solar and Corning subsidiary American Panel Solutions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/first-solar-sues-ja-solar-and-american-panel-solutions-over-topcon-patents/\">First Solar sues JA Solar and American Panel Solutions over TOPCon patents</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-maga", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/first-solar-sues-ja-solar-and-american-panel-solutions-over-topcon-patents/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-011", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Next2Sun files for insolvency for two subsidiaries", "content": "<p>German vertical PV specialist Next2Sun has filed for self-administered insolvency proceedings for two subsidiaries after failing to secure €5 million in fresh capital. The company says project development activities will continue, while it seeks new investors and explores restructuring options.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/next2sun-files-for-insolvency-for-two-subsidiaries/\">Next2Sun files for insolvency for two subsidiaries</a> appeared first on <a href=\"ht", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/next2sun-files-for-insolvency-for-two-subsidiaries/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-012", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China’s 700 MW Jintan salt-cavern CAES project completes full-system startup", "content": "<p>The two-unit non-fuel CAES project is now moving toward grid-connection testing and system commissioning. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/chinas-700-mw-jintan-salt-cavern-caes-project-completes-full-system-startup/\">China’s 700 MW Jintan salt-cavern CAES project completes full-system startup</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/chinas-700-mw-jintan-salt-cavern-caes-project-completes-full-system-startup/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-013", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Perovskite may leak less lead than lead-solder silicon, say scientists", "content": "<p>A model of perovskite deployment in China to 2060 finds that lead is no barrier to commercialization if properly managed, but warns that exported modules could shift a disproportionate share of leakage to tropical developing countries.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/perovskite-may-leak-less-lead-than-lead-solder-silicon-say-scientists/\">Perovskite may leak less lead than lead-solder silicon, say scientists</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/perovskite-may-leak-less-lead-than-lead-solder-silicon-say-scientists/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-014", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Digital twin tech offers ‘anti-involution’ strategies for China’s PV industry", "content": "<p>Researchers in China have developed a digital twin-based simulation framework to help PV manufacturers counter excessive price competition and declining profitability. The study found that combining moderate price increases with higher R&#38;D investment could improve financial performance and long-term competitiveness, although the results remain unvalidated in real-world operations.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/digital-twin-tech-offers-anti-involution-stra", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/digital-twin-tech-offers-anti-involution-strategies-for-chinas-pv-industry/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-015", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU grants cross-border solar, wind project priority status", "content": "<p>The Deploy project plans to build 180 MW of solar and wind in Poland, with the electricity generated to be converted into heat for industrial offtakers in Germany.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/eu-grants-cross-border-solar-wind-project-priority-status/\">EU grants cross-border solar, wind project priority status</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/eu-grants-cross-border-solar-wind-project-priority-status/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-016", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Silver-nickel contacts cut TOPCon rear metallization costs by 11%", "content": "<p>Chinese researchers developed a screen-printed silver-nickel paste that reduces rear-side metallization costs by approximately 11%. The optimized formulation achieved an average cell efficiency of 26.67% in a production trial, with a champion device reaching 26.87%.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/silver-nickel-contacts-cut-topcon-rear-metallization-costs-by-11/\">Silver-nickel contacts cut TOPCon rear metallization costs by 11%</a> appeared first on <a href=\"ht", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/silver-nickel-contacts-cut-topcon-rear-metallization-costs-by-11/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-017", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Perovskite solar cell based on Prussian blue achieves 26.9% efficiency", "content": "<p>Chinese researchers have used Prussian Blue nanoparticles to improve the efficiency and stability of perovskite solar cells, achieving efficiencies of up to 26.9%. The approach also enabled the fabrication of large-area modules with certified efficiencies of 22.9% and promising results in accelerated aging and outdoor stability tests.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/perovskite-solar-cell-based-on-prussian-blue-achieves-26-9-efficiency/\">Perovskite solar cell ba", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/10/05/perovskite-solar-cell-based-on-prussian-blue-achieves-26-9-efficiency/", "type": "rss"}]}
