{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-030", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solar on Staten Island affordable housing serves community and tenants Solar Power World’s Projects of Impact", "content": "<p>The Sisters of Charity of New York, a Catholic mission group that has spearheaded healthcare and affordable housing developments in the state, called on the power of the sun to reduce energy costs for elderly tenants in a Staten Island housing complex. PV consultancy firm Crauderueff Solar helped the mission group develop an adequate solar&#8230;</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/10/solar-on-staten-island-affordable-housing-serves-community-and-tentants/\">Sol", "sources": [{"name": "solar_power_world", "url": "https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/10/solar-on-staten-island-affordable-housing-serves-community-and-tentants/", "type": "rss"}]}
