{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-032", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Why NERC compliance starts in solar project design", "content": "<p>For grid-scale solar projects connecting to the bulk electric system, NERC compliance is often treated as a post-construction concern, when the obligations take shape much earlier in the design phase. Waiting until commissioning to address compliance can leave owner-operators scrambling at the commercial operation date (COD), when full regulatory responsibility activates. Facilities with a rating&#8230;</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/10/why-nerc-compliance", "sources": [{"name": "solar_power_world", "url": "https://www.solarpowerworldonline.com/2026/10/why-nerc-compliance-starts-in-solar-project-design/", "type": "rss"}]}
